<title>USA: Polaroid to use Creo Products machines.</title>
<headline>Polaroid to use Creo Products machines.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass. 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polaroid Corp said Wednesday its graphics imaging division has entered into an agreement to use Creo Products Inc's computer-to-plate machines for use in printing Polaroid's dry, digital film.</p>
<p>The agreement allows Polaroid's Dry Tech Imagesetting film to be printed on Creo's line of Trendsetters, the company said.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Creo Products Inc is based in Burnaby, British Columbia.</p>
